Parámetros publicados: External size (LxW):: 2160x980 mm±10mm; Mattress platform:: 1930x830 mm; Safe workingload:: 200 kg; Height adjustment:: 505 mm; Back-rest adjustment:: 0-80°(±10°); Knee-rest adjustment:: 0-35°(±10°); Manual Cranks: 2pcs; 5" Covered Castors: 4pcs; Foldable Side Rail: 1set; PP Bed Ends with Safe Lock: 1set; IV Pole: 1set; IV Pole Prevision: 4pcs; Drainage Hook: 2pcs; Comparison Dimension: Hospital Manual Bed Key Advantages; Procurement Cost: Significantly lower cost. A hospital manual bed typically costs 1/3 to 1/5 of electric models, making it ideal for budget-sensitive healthcare projects, home care, and bulk hospital procurement.; Power & Environment: Fully independent from electricity. The manual hospital bed can be used in rural hospitals, emergency situations, or areas with unstable power supply without any limitation.; Reliability & Maintenance: High mechanical reliability with a simple crank system. The hospital manual bed has fewer failure points and requires minimal maintenance throughout its service life.; Operation Safety: Designed to reduce patient misoperation risk. Adjustment is controlled by caregivers, making the manual hospital bed safer for elderly, unconscious, or post-operative patients.; Mobility & Weight: Lightweight structure without motor or battery components, making the manual hospital bed easier to move within wards or home care environments.; Maintenance Cost: Extremely low long-term maintenance cost. Simple mechanical components ensure durability and reduce replacement frequency.; Suitable Scenarios: Ideal for general wards, short-term recovery, home care, rural healthcare projects, and cost-sensitive hospital procurement.; Adjustment Experience: Manual crank adjustment may require physical effort but provides stable and predictable positioning for patient care.; Core Value Positioning: The hospital manual bed focuses on affordability, durability, safety, and independence from electricity, making it a practical solution for essential patient care..

